T7 - Treasury and grants (ECONOMICS_PLAN, W4). Gate literally: every payout has proposal + tx + report - each executed payout carries the authorizing proposal (state Executed), a numbered tx and a transparent Report {tx_id, proposal_id, amount, recipient, purpose, height}; a withdrawal without a passed vote is rejected (NoVote). Council 5 votes payout proposals (strict majority), the multisig of 3 requires 2 approvals (decision W4); the lifecycle is propose -> vote -> finalize -> approve -> execute. The treasury cannot overdraw (signed i128 balance; conservation final + paid = initial + inflows), a payout cannot execute twice (AlreadyExecuted), a rejected proposal never pays (Rejected). Pinned scenario: 10 grant proposals / 82 steps / 6 payouts (tx 1..6), final balance 225 000 ALCRY, 475 000 ALCRY paid; golden digest 719c93b244ff42ebf94538a5e9fb5b9e8f52eac07035abaf3c526e4c0a3231f7 pinned in Rust tests and re-derived by the independent Python oracle (tools/t7_treasury_check.py), which cross-runs t7_treasury_example. NC: 7/7 named messages (tools/nc_t7.py; standard 6 + the literal withdrawal-without-vote rejection). 10 gate tests + 2 metamorphisms. Evidence docs/evidence/t7 (565 NCs cumulative over 24 phases). ALL GATES GREEN.

